  "notes": [
    "First focused frontend run was stopped during lengthy discovery; actual Vitest config now excludes generated Rust output, scratch and evidence while retaining all existing script/spike tests.",
    "An earlier full run passed 395 tests; a later run hit the default one-second lazy-editor lookup timeout. Only that lookup received a bounded ten-second wait; all assertions remain.",
    "Clippy rejected a large navigation enum and needless borrowed str references; boxed the request without changing JSON and removed both unnecessary borrows.",
    "Default axe caught low contrast on raised card-label tracks and labelled generic divs. Reused the existing dark secondary text token and added group roles; no axe rule was disabled.",
    "The premature first flow overlapped a build and never loaded the app. Its owned bridge was stopped through test.stop; its failed report/raw log remain. The accepted flow runs only after a completed build.",
    "Original parser behavior, including date-normalization quirks, is retained; unsupported project/assignee resolution stays literal and GitHub repository detection becomes a normal bookmark.",
    "Frozen parse clock and per-edited-draft UUID make unchanged retries deterministic; remounted views acknowledge saved IDs from the authoritative scoped card snapshot.",
    "The light tray key hint also needed the existing secondary text tone. All contrast/semantic failures remain archived; default axe finishes with zero violations and incomplete results.",
    "A focused checklist screenshot failed the exact-repeat assertion. After verifying its initial field focus, the capture verifier now follows the existing editor policy: focus Close and leave the caret unmodified. No repeat assertion was disabled.",
    "Axe spatial-grid diagnostics found an empty outgoing animation element retaining a box after cleanup. Hiding only :empty layers fixes that overlap while populated crossfades keep their existing behavior; no axe exception was added.",
    "Visual comparison found inherited centered recent-card headings and input font inheritance. Explicit leading alignment, zero letter spacing and 13px capture type now match the design. Typography checks use effective font values and the leading dot offset; the browser serializes flex-start as flow-start, so geometry is the alignment proof.",
    "Lint caught an unqualified browser getComputedStyle in the new verifier; it now uses globalThis. A subsequent full verify and final lint pass."
  ]
